# index.html is generated by build.js and byte-compared by `build.js --check`.
# Normalising every text file the same way keeps that comparison valid on both
# Windows checkouts (CRLF) and Linux CI (LF) — what matters is that the template,
# the sources and the built artifact all agree.
* text=auto

# Vendored third-party builds are the exception: they are byte-for-byte upstream
# artefacts, and vendor/README.md records their checksums so an update can be shown
# to be the real file. Normalisation rewrites those bytes and makes the checksums
# wrong, which is exactly what happened when they were first committed.
vendor/*.js -text
